---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Button from "../components/ui/Button.astro";
import officerPhoto from "../assets/about/officer-sia-badge.png";

/**
 * About page — first build. `/about` was already a live, nav-linked
 * route (Header.astro, NavDrawer.tsx, and MissionBand.astro's own "More
 * about us" button all already point here) with no page file behind it
 * until now.
 *
 * CONTENT — supplied verbatim by the user (the intro copy, the three
 * bullets, and the Mission/Services/Vision sections), lightly adapted
 * only for on-page flow: the Services paragraph's flat comma-separated
 * service list is broken out into a wrapped inline row for readability
 * (same sentence, same words, no descriptors invented per service —
 * see the SERVICES section comment below for why 3 of the 9 named
 * services have no matching icon file and are rendered as plain text
 * rather than forcing a mismatched icon set).
 *
 * IMAGE — `src/assets/about/officer-sia-badge.png` (1024×1536, real
 * geometry confirmed via `sharp` metadata, not guessed), a real,
 * final, House-of-Guards-branded photograph supplied by the user — a
 * uniformed officer, front-facing, wearing an SIA licence badge on a
 * lanyard, blurred Bradford street/plaza background. Not a placeholder
 * — flagged here only for provenance, same convention as
 * `hero-officer.png`/`mission-team.png`. Deliberately paired with the
 * "SIA licensed and DBS checked officers" bullet in the same section —
 * the badge is legible in the photo itself, so the image corroborates
 * the claim rather than just illustrating the page generically.
 * Rendered at its own native 2:3 ratio (`aspect-[2/3]`), uncropped —
 * `object-cover` at a matching ratio performs no real crop, it's a
 * robustness net only, same discipline as every other real photo on
 * this site.
 *
 * COLOUR — deliberately restrained to ONE accent moment, not the full
 * four-colour rebrand vocabulary. This page is a new, non-homepage
 * section, so per CLAUDE.md's own hard-rule text it only gets Electric
 * Blue/Magenta if a fresh, explicit instruction extends the palette
 * here — the task brief that produced this page named "Electric Blue,
 * Magenta, Amber-only-CTA" as available tokens, which is exactly that
 * kind of explicit extension. Used narrowly: Electric Blue for ONE
 * full-bleed band (Our Mission), Amber for the one CTA button, nothing
 * else — Magenta is deliberately NOT used anywhere on this page; there
 * was no second, distinct colour moment the content actually called
 * for, and reaching for Magenta just because it was available would be
 * exactly the "colour on every section because it's there" default
 * this brief asked to avoid. CLAUDE.md's own palette-scope note is
 * updated in the same commit to record About as a further named,
 * narrow exception (Electric Blue only, one band), matching how
 * SectorsGrid's own carve-out was documented.
 *
 * Mission band: white/Paper text on Electric Blue reuses the
 * already-derived ~5.17:1 (AA) pairing from global.css's own token
 * comment — no new contrast maths needed, same fill/foreground
 * combination StatStrip/Header's info bar/ServicesGrid's coloured
 * cards already use. `.on-dark` is applied defensively (no focusable
 * element inside the band today, matching ServicesGrid's own
 * precedent for a fill with no interactive content).
 *
 * MOTION — exactly one deliberate moment, not motion on every section,
 * per the brief's own explicit ask. Only the Mission band gets a
 * scroll reveal (`[data-reveal]`, reusing the plain generic
 * `scrollReveal.ts` module directly — the same one StatStrip and
 * StandardsCarousel already reuse unmodified, no new bespoke motion
 * module needed for a single plain fade/rise band). The intro section
 * and the Services/Vision sections are static — no entrance animation,
 * so the one motion beat this page has actually reads as deliberate
 * rather than default page furniture.
 *
 * ALIGNMENT — left throughout, the sitewide default. No section on
 * this page centres itself; there was no instruction or established
 * precedent (beyond SectorsGrid's own narrow, differently-shaped
 * heading-only exception) that would justify one here.
 *
 * SERVICES — the source paragraph names 9 services, but only 6 of this
 * project's bespoke service icons exist (`src/icons/services/*`,
 * matching ServicesGrid.astro's own 6 cards). Rather than force a
 * mismatched icon set (6 icons for 9 names) or invent 3 new bespoke
 * icons as unrequested scope, the service list renders as plain text —
 * a wrapped row of names separated by a thin hairline dot, no icons at
 * all on this page. Flagged here rather than silently deciding either
 * way.
 *
 * CTA TARGET — `/#quote-form`, landing directly on ClosingCta's own
 * quote-request card rather than just the homepage top. `/contact` has
 * no page file yet (a known, disclosed gap — see CLAUDE.md's own "Not
 * started" list), so `/` is still the right destination; ClosingCta.
 * astro previously had no `id` anywhere in its markup to hash-link to
 * (confirmed at first build), so a minimal `id="quote-form"` was added
 * directly to its floating "Get A Quote" card — the one addition
 * `ClosingCta.astro` needed, nothing else in that file touched.
 */
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="House of Guards is a young, Bradford-based physical security company founded in 2023 — SIA-licensed, DBS-checked officers delivering manned guarding, close protection, and CCTV monitoring across West Yorkshire."
>
  <section class="bg-paper">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-gutter py-20 md:px-12 md:py-28">
      <h1 class="text-h1 text-ink max-w-2xl">About House of Guards</h1>
      <p class="text-h3 text-ink mt-3 max-w-2xl">A young company with experienced people</p>

      <div class="mt-12 grid grid-cols-1 items-start gap-12 md:grid-cols-2 md:gap-16 lg:gap-20">
        <div class="text-left">
          <p class="text-body-lg text-ink max-w-md">
            House of Guards is a new establishment formed in 2023, working across the
            sectors listed on our Services page. We are growing steadily in both staff
            and contracts, and we continue to recruit skilled SIA licensed officers,
            CCTV monitoring operators and stewards.
          </p>
          <p class="text-body text-ink mt-5 max-w-md">
            Most of our work takes place in West Yorkshire, though some shifts run
            further afield with transport provided. Our staff receive regular training
            on how to sharpen their work, because professionalism is central to how we
            operate — and to what we expect from every member of the crew.
          </p>

          <ul class="mt-8 max-w-md divide-y divide-hairline border-t border-hairline">
            <li class="py-4 text-body text-ink">SIA licensed and DBS checked officers</li>
            <li class="py-4 text-body text-ink">First aid trained personnel</li>
            <li class="py-4 text-body text-ink">Bespoke shift patterns, arranged around you</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="aspect-[2/3] overflow-hidden md:max-w-sm md:justify-self-end">
          <Image
            src={officerPhoto}
            alt="A House of Guards security officer in a branded jacket, wearing an SIA licence badge on a lanyard, standing on a Bradford street"
            class="h-full w-full object-cover"
            widths={[320, 480, 640, 768]}
            sizes="(min-width: 768px) 24rem, 100vw"
            format="webp"
            quality={82}
            loading="eager"
          />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="on-dark bg-electric-blue" data-reveal>
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-gutter py-20 md:px-12 md:py-24">
      <h2 class="text-h2 text-paper max-w-2xl">Our mission</h2>
      <p class="text-body-lg text-paper mt-5 max-w-2xl">
        To meet our clients' needs to perfection in a professional working
        environment, and to recruit staff who share those values. We aim to give
        full assurance in the safety our guards provide, and to become a leading
        supplier of reliable close protection officers in the North.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-paper">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-gutter py-20 md:px-12 md:py-24">
      <h2 class="text-h2 text-ink max-w-2xl">Our services</h2>
      <p class="text-body-lg text-ink mt-5 max-w-2xl">
        We deliver:
      </p>
      <ul class="mt-4 flex max-w-2xl flex-wrap items-center gap-x-3 gap-y-2" aria-label="Services we offer">
        {[
          "Corporate security",
          "Close protection",
          "CCTV monitoring",
          "Manned guarding",
          "Retail security",
          "Construction site security",
          "Overnight security",
          "Private property security",
          "Event stewarding",
        ].map((service, i) => (
          <>
            {i > 0 && <span class="text-stone select-none" aria-hidden="true">·</span>}
            <li class="text-body text-ink">{service}</li>
          </>
        ))}
      </ul>
      <p class="text-body text-ink mt-5 max-w-2xl">
        Bespoke arrangements are available, and our specialists are operational
        24 hours a day.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-paper">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-gutter py-20 md:px-12 md:py-28">
      <h2 class="text-h2 text-ink max-w-2xl">Our vision</h2>
      <p class="text-body-lg text-ink mt-5 max-w-md">
        To offer the best quality for the right price. We invest in our people so
        they can outperform the rest, commit to ongoing improvement in every area,
        and build a team of experts who understand our core values and want to
        deliver on them.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-8">
        <Button href="/#quote-form">Get in touch</Button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <script>
    import { initScrollReveal } from "../lib/scrollReveal";

    document.addEventListener("astro:page-load", () => {
      initScrollReveal();
    });
  </script>
</BaseLayout>
